# SMS intake — fixture name ≠ location

**Symptom (Adriana):** Tenant texts `My faucet is dripping`. Ulo skips “Which room…?” and jumps to photo / entry / confirm. The ticket has no kitchen vs bathroom, so the vendor probe and dashboard cannot tell which faucet.

## Rule

A fixture word is **not** a room. Location is known only when `resolveRoomLabel(state)` returns a room (from `room_or_area` or text like “kitchen sink”).

| Text | Location known? | Ask `room_or_area`? |
|---|---|---|
| `My faucet is dripping` | No | **Yes** |
| `Kitchen faucet is dripping` | Yes (kitchen) | No |
| `My sink is clogged` | No | **Yes** (after overflow triage) |
| `Bathroom sink leaking` | Yes (bathroom) | No |
| `I have no water` / whole-home outage | Scope ask, not room | Scope question instead |

## Autofix (Bugbot)

On PR review or when this pattern appears in chat / SMS thread dumps:

1. **Never** skip `room_or_area` because `hasFixture(hay)` matched (`faucet`, `sink`, `toilet`, `shower`, `tub`, appliance, outlet, …).
2. Gate the room ask on `!resolveRoomLabel(state)` (and non-HVAC / non-lock / non-door paths) — not on “fixture already named.”
3. Whole-home outage / hot-water scope questions remain the location ask for those cases (`matchesWholeHomeWaterOutage`); do not also force a redundant room ask after “everywhere in the home.”
4. Add/extend a Deno test: `"My faucet is dripping"` → `questionType === "room_or_area"`; `"Kitchen faucet is dripping"` → not `room_or_area`.

## Canonical helpers

| Concern | Module |
|---|---|
| Next question order | `determineNextMaintenanceQuestion.ts` |
| Room extraction | `resolveRoomLabel` / `extractRoomFromText` in `residentIntakeTypes.ts` |
| Whole-home outage | `matchesWholeHomeWaterOutage` in `deterministicRules.ts` |

## Do not

- Treat fixture vocabulary as answering “where”
- Jump to photo / confirm while `resolveRoomLabel` is null for a fixture-only report
- Re-introduce `!hasFixture(hay)` on the `room_or_area` gate
- Ask room again after the resident already said the water is out everywhere